    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Create balanced hackathon teams using this student data:\n\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.data) }}\n\nYou are an expert hackathon team formation assistant.\n\nObjective:\nCreate the strongest possible hackathon teams while satisfying all constraints.\n\nConstraints:\n\nTeam size must be exactly 4 members.\nEvery student must be assigned exactly once.\nNo duplicate assignments.\nEach team should have a balanced mix of skills.\nDistribute experienced members evenly across teams.\nAvoid placing all beginners in one team.\nIf available, each team should contain:\nAt least one technical member (Programming/AI/Web/App Development)\nAt least one design or presentation-oriented member\nAvoid putting students with identical skill sets together when possible.\nMaximize diversity of skills within each team.\nIf the total number of students is not divisible by 4, create the minimum number of teams possible and distribute remaining members fairly.\n\nAssign one role per member:\n\nTeam Lead\nBackend Developer\nFrontend Developer\nAI/ML Engineer\nUI/UX Designer\nResearcher\nPresenter\nFull Stack Developer\n\n\n\n\n\nReturn ONLY raw JSON.\n\nDo not add explanations.\nDo not add markdown.\nDo not use code blocks.\nDo not use ```json.\n\nThe response must start with {\nThe response must end with }\n\nOutput format:\n\n{\n  \"teams\": [\n    {\n      \"team_name\": \"Team 1\",\n      \"members\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"\",\n          \"email\": \"\",\n          \"phone\": \"\",\n          \"role\": \"\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "batching": {
          "batchSize": 35
        }
      },
